  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 95,
    "summary": "Let us sing unto the Lord—Let us worship and bow down before Him—Israel provoked the Lord and failed to enter into His rest.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "O come, let us sing unto the Lord: let us make a joyful noise to the rock of our salvation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "1 Chr. 16:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Ps. 66:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "2 Sam. 22:47; Ps. 89:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, and make a joyful noise unto him with psalms.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "TG Thanksgiving."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the Lord is a great God, and a great King above all gods.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "1 Chr. 16:25."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "TG Kingdom of God, in Heaven."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 15
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In his hand are the deep places of the earth: the strength of the hills is his also.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The sea is his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O come, let us worship and bow down: let us kneel before the Lord our maker.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Worship."
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "Ps. 149:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For he is our God; and we are the people of his pasture, and the sheep of his hand. To day if ye will hear his voice,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Good Shepherd; Sheep."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "Heb. 3:7 (7–11)."
          },
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "Heb. 4:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "D&C 88:66."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Harden not your heart, as in the provocation, and as in the day of temptation in the wilderness:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Hardheartedness."
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "HEB at Meribah."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "TG Provoking."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "TG Test."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my work.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Test."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Forty years long was I grieved with this generation, and said, It is a people that do err in their heart, and they have not known my ways:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "Num. 14:33; Deut. 2:14 (14–15)."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "Ps. 119:158."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Prov. 30:12 (11–14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Unto whom I sware in my wrath that they should not enter into my rest.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "Heb. 3:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG God, Privilege of Seeing; Rest."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
